{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "meta": {
    "id": "art_major-vs-minor",
    "slug": "major-vs-minor",
    "title": "Major vs Minor",
    "summary": "How the two scales are built, and the three notes that change everything.",
    "tags": ["theory"],
    "readingTimeMin": 3,
    "publishedAt": "2026-08-02"
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        { "text": "Almost every song you know lives in one of two moods: " },
        { "text": "major", "marks": ["bold", { "type": "color", "tone": "accent" }] },
        { "text": " or " },
        { "text": "minor", "marks": ["bold", { "type": "color", "tone": "amber" }] },
        { "text": ". Built from the same root, they differ by exactly " },
        { "text": "three notes", "link": { "kind": "footnote", "id": "fn-parallel" } },
        { "text": " — and once you can hear those three, you hear the difference everywhere." }
      ]
    },
    { "type": "heading", "level": 1, "spans": [{ "text": "Two recipes, one root" }] },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        { "text": "A scale is a recipe of whole and half steps. The major scale climbs " },
        { "text": "W–W–H–W–W–W–H", "marks": ["code"] },
        { "text": "; the natural minor climbs " },
        { "text": "W–H–W–W–H–W–W", "marks": ["code"] },
        {
          "text": ". Same ingredients, different order — and the order is the mood.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        [
          { "text": "Major", "marks": ["bold"] },
          { "text": " — bright, settled, sure of where home is." }
        ],
        [
          { "text": "Minor", "marks": ["bold"] },
          { "text": " — darker, unresolved, leaning inward." }
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "header": [[{ "text": "Degree" }], [{ "text": "Major" }], [{ "text": "Minor" }]],
      "rows": [
        [
          [{ "text": "Third" }],
          [{ "text": "3", "marks": ["code"] }],
          [{ "text": "b3", "marks": ["code"] }]
        ],
        [
          [{ "text": "Sixth" }],
          [{ "text": "6", "marks": ["code"] }],
          [{ "text": "b6", "marks": ["code"] }]
        ],
        [
          [{ "text": "Seventh" }],
          [{ "text": "7", "marks": ["code"] }],
          [{ "text": "b7", "marks": ["code"] }]
        ]
      ]
    },
    { "type": "heading", "level": 1, "spans": [{ "text": "Hear it" }] },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Both scales below start from the same root, A. Tap play on each and listen for the third note — the tones tinted "
        },
        { "text": "amber", "marks": [{ "type": "color", "tone": "amber" }] },
        { "text": " are the ones minor lowers." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "live",
      "component": "scale-compare",
      "props": { "root": "A", "scales": ["major", "minor"] }
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "tone": "tip",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Play the major run, then immediately the minor one. The mood flips on the third note — that's the "
        },
        { "text": "b3", "marks": ["code"] },
        { "text": " doing the work." }
      ]
    },
    { "type": "divider" },
    { "type": "heading", "level": 2, "spans": [{ "text": "Where to go next" }] },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        { "text": "Map either scale across the whole neck in the " },
        { "text": "Scale Visualizer", "link": { "kind": "screen", "href": "/scale-visualizer" } },
        { "text": ", or read about " },
        {
          "text": "relative keys",
          "link": { "kind": "url", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Relative_key" }
        },
        { "text": " — the other way major and minor are entangled." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "quote",
      "spans": [{ "text": "The minor scale is the major scale wearing its heart on its sleeve." }],
      "attribution": "Every theory teacher, eventually"
    }
  ],
  "footnotes": [
    {
      "id": "fn-parallel",
      "spans": [
        { "text": "Comparing scales on the same root — A major against A minor — is a " },
        { "text": "parallel", "marks": ["italic"] },
        {
          "text": " comparison. Relative comparison (C major against A minor) shares the notes and moves the root instead."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
